<title>SINGAPORE: Hong Kong Land hits new year high.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong Land hits new year high.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in property company Hong Kong Land Holdings hit a new year high of US$2.45, up 11 cents, on Monday in heavy volume, dealers said.</p>
<p>The rise followed a new record close on Hong Kong's Hang Seng Index of 13,042.80 points, up 153.43.</p>
<p>Volume for the company was 7.26 million shares.</p>
<p>Dealers said there was no obvious reason why the stock was performing so strongly, but said the rise could have been linked to hopes that Hong Kong's new chief executive after the handover to China from Britain would have links to the property market.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
